# SCSS RWD and Git Rules

## Styling

* Use SCSS.
* Prefer scoped SCSS.
* Use existing mixins when available.
* Do not introduce TailwindCSS unless requested.
* Avoid inline styles.

## Responsive Design

All pages should support:

* desktop
* tablet
* mobile

Prefer:

* flex
* grid
* percentage width
* max-width
* SCSS mixins

Avoid:

* unnecessary fixed width
* desktop-only layout
* hardcoded mobile hacks

## Git Commit

Use Conventional Commit format.

Examples:

```txt
feat(home): add banner carousel
fix(wallet): resolve withdraw validation
refactor(api): optimize request handling
style(home): adjust mobile spacing
chore(config): update vite settings
```

Rules:

* Commit message must be in English.
* Review git diff before committing.
* Suggest commit message first.
* Do not push automatically unless explicitly requested.
* If changes are unrelated, suggest splitting into multiple commits.
